window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b243-676f584d0c97a896.json"]={sha256:"676f584d0c97a8969985c3528ec1c9b1bca199c54d1c5cd8824b3621c653f4f2",value:{"id":"b243","title":"水庫邊坡穩定監測","titleEn":"Reservoir-slope stability monitoring","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以整合庫水位降雨孔壓與三維位移判讀邊坡為主線，先用有效應力與孔壓與無限邊坡力學示意界定水力與構造條件，再將衛星定位共同誤差、位移速率與加速度連結到監測不確定與應變。以合成邊坡作機制識別，無法由單一位移序列預測崩塌時間或湧浪。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops integrating reservoir stage rainfall pore pressure and three-dimensional slope displacement through Effective stress and pore pressure and Infinite slope force illustration, then connects GNSS common-mode errors and Displacement rate and acceleration to Monitoring uncertainty and response. Synthetic slopes illustrate mechanisms; a single displacement series cannot predict failure time or impulse waves. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["有效應力與孔壓","Effective stress and pore pressure"],["水文傳遞時間尺度","Hydrological diffusion time scale"],["衛星定位共同誤差","GNSS common-mode errors"],["位移速率與加速度","Displacement rate and acceleration"],["監測不確定與應變","Monitoring uncertainty and response"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["有效應力與孔壓","水文傳遞時間尺度","衛星定位共同誤差","位移速率與加速度","監測不確定與應變"],"labelsEn":["Effective stress and pore pressure","Hydrological diffusion time scale","GNSS common-mode errors","Displacement rate and acceleration","Monitoring uncertainty and response"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查有效應力與孔壓：sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa；再獨立檢查無限邊坡力學示意：Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348。敏感度：相同總正應力150kPa下，孔壓由60增為90kPa，有效正應力由90降為60kPa；固定摩擦角30度時摩擦抗力由51.96降為34.64kPa，減少三分之一。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。以合成邊坡作機制識別，無法由單一位移序列預測崩塌時間或湧浪。 將對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Effective stress and pore pressure: sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa. Independently examine Infinite slope force illustration: Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348. Sensitivity: at total normal stress150kPa, raising pore pressure from60 to90kPa reduces effective normal stress from90 to60kPa. With a fixed30-degree friction angle, frictional resistance decreases from51.96 to34.64kPa, a one-third reduction. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Synthetic slopes illustrate mechanisms; a single displacement series cannot predict failure time or impulse waves. Use the following independent check: Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b243-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「有效應力與孔壓」與「無限邊坡力學示意」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Effective stress and pore pressure\" and \"Infinite slope force illustration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b243-v15-01","title":"有效應力與孔壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective stress and pore pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「有效應力與孔壓」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective stress and pore pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水庫邊坡的抗剪能力受滑面有效正應力控制，外部水位下降可能移除坡腳水壓支撐，內部孔壓卻尚未消散。必須將坡內孔壓與滑面總應力分開估計，不能只用庫水位替代；簡化摩擦式也忽略了吸力、軟化與漸進破壞。 驗證時應將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較，並辨識以下失效情境：孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效應力與孔壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Slope resistance depends on effective normal stress. Falling reservoir stage may remove external support before internal pressure dissipates. Estimate total stress and slip-surface pore pressure separately rather than replacing internal head with reservoir level; the simple friction law also omits suction, softening and progressive failure. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective stress and pore pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效應力與孔壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective stress and pore pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-01-k1","title":"有效應力與孔壓","titleEn":"Effective stress and pore pressure","text":"水庫邊坡的抗剪能力受滑面有效正應力控制，外部水位下降可能移除坡腳水壓支撐，內部孔壓卻尚未消散。必須將坡內孔壓與滑面總應力分開估計，不能只用庫水位替代；簡化摩擦式也忽略了吸力、軟化與漸進破壞。","textEn":"Slope resistance depends on effective normal stress. Falling reservoir stage may remove external support before internal pressure dissipates.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「有效應力與孔壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective stress and pore pressure\" is correct?","options":["庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低","水庫邊坡的抗剪能力受滑面有效正應力控制，外部水位下降可能移除坡腳水壓支撐，內部孔壓卻尚未消散。","示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全"],"optionsEn":["Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction","Slope resistance depends on effective normal stress.","An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope"],"answer":1,"explanation":"水庫邊坡的抗剪能力受滑面有效正應力控制，外部水位下降可能移除坡腳水壓支撐，內部孔壓卻尚未消散。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Slope resistance depends on effective normal stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b243-v15-02","title":"有效應力與孔壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective stress and pore pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效應力與孔壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective stress and pore pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「有效應力與孔壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective stress and pore pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準","雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移","原創教學假設：sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference","Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement","Original teaching assumptions: sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: sigmaNormal=150 kPa; u=60 kPa; phi=30 degrees; friction=(150-60)*tan(30 degrees)=51.9615 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b243-v15-03","title":"有效應力與孔壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective stress and pore pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效應力與孔壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective stress and pore pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「有效應力與孔壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective stress and pore pressure\"?","options":["將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率"],"optionsEn":["Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b243-v15-04","title":"有效應力與孔壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective stress and pore pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效應力與孔壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective stress and pore pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力。診斷時應採取以下查核：將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. Diagnose it by the following check: Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力。診斷時應採取以下查核：將滑面附近孔壓時序與庫水位下降段對齊比較，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. Diagnose it by the following check: Align pore pressures near the potential slip surface with reservoir drawdown intervals. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「有效應力與孔壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective stress and pore pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力。","示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance.","An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔壓消散慢於外水位下降可降低有效抗剪能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pore pressure lagging external drawdown can reduce available shear resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b243-v15-05","title":"無限邊坡力學示意：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Infinite slope force illustration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「無限邊坡力學示意」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Infinite slope force illustration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻無限邊坡把重量分解為沿坡驅動與垂直坡面的正力，適合展示厚度、坡角與孔壓的作用，不能代表複雜旋轉滑動。所用深度須明定為垂直深度，否則三角函數形式不同；有側向約束與分層時應改用合適的分析模型。 驗證時應以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗，並辨識以下失效情境：把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「無限邊坡力學示意」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An infinite-slope idealization resolves weight into driving and normal components, illustrating depth, angle and pore-pressure effects without representing rotational slides. Specify vertical depth because slope-normal thickness produces different geometry. Lateral confinement, layering and curved slip surfaces require a different analysis rather than hidden adjustments to this equation. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Infinite slope force illustration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348.","failure":"常見誤解：「示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「無限邊坡力學示意」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Infinite slope force illustration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-05-k1","title":"無限邊坡力學示意","titleEn":"Infinite slope force illustration","text":"均勻無限邊坡把重量分解為沿坡驅動與垂直坡面的正力，適合展示厚度、坡角與孔壓的作用，不能代表複雜旋轉滑動。所用深度須明定為垂直深度，否則三角函數形式不同；有側向約束與分層時應改用合適的分析模型。","textEn":"An infinite-slope idealization resolves weight into driving and normal components, illustrating depth, angle and pore-pressure effects without representing rotational slides. Specify vertical depth because slope-normal thickness produces different geometry.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「無限邊坡力學示意」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Infinite slope force illustration\" is correct?","options":["示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全","水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數","均勻無限邊坡把重量分解為沿坡驅動與垂直坡面的正力，適合展示厚度、坡角與孔壓的作用，不能代表複雜旋轉滑動。"],"optionsEn":["An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope","The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown","An infinite-slope idealization resolves weight into driving and normal components, illustrating depth, angle and pore-pressure effects without representing rotational slides."],"answer":2,"explanation":"均勻無限邊坡把重量分解為沿坡驅動與垂直坡面的正力，適合展示厚度、坡角與孔壓的作用，不能代表複雜旋轉滑動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An infinite-slope idealization resolves weight into driving and normal components, illustrating depth, angle and pore-pressure effects without representing rotational slides. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b243-v15-06","title":"無限邊坡力學示意：定量估算","titleEn":"Infinite slope force illustration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「無限邊坡力學示意」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Infinite slope force illustration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「無限邊坡力學示意」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Infinite slope force illustration\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348。","相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移","短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348.","Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated","Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Dry cohesionless slope: phi=32 degrees; beta=24 degrees; FS=tan(32 degrees)/tan(24 degrees)=1.40348. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b243-v15-07","title":"無限邊坡力學示意：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Infinite slope force illustration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「無限邊坡力學示意」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Infinite slope force illustration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「無限邊坡力學示意」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Infinite slope force illustration\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗。","只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently.","Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b243-v15-08","title":"無限邊坡力學示意：失效診斷","titleEn":"Infinite slope force illustration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「無限邊坡力學示意」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Infinite slope force illustration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比。診斷時應採取以下查核：以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. Diagnose it by the following check: Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比。診斷時應採取以下查核：以剖面地形確認平行滑面假設並對摩擦角做獨立試驗，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. Diagnose it by the following check: Check the parallel-plane assumption against cross-sections and test friction angle independently. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「無限邊坡力學示意」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Infinite slope force illustration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數","把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown","Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把乾燥簡式套在高孔壓層會高估抗滑比。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the dry expression in a high-pressure layer overstates resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b243-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「水文傳遞時間尺度」與「測斜積分與基準」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Hydrological diffusion time scale\" and \"Inclinometer integration and reference\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b243-v15-09","title":"水文傳遞時間尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hydrological diffusion time scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「水文傳遞時間尺度」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydrological diffusion time scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"降雨與庫水位會透過不同通道影響孔壓，擴散時間約隨距離平方增加，因此深層反應可能晚於地表事件。特徵時間只給量級，裂縫對流、非飽和入滲與變動邊界均會偏離均質擴散；應用多深度觀測區分傳遞機制。 驗證時應比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄，並辨識以下失效情境：把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水文傳遞時間尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Rainfall and reservoir stage influence pressures through different pathways. A diffusion time scale grows with distance squared, so deep response may lag surface forcing. This is an order-of-magnitude estimate; fracture advection, unsaturated infiltration and moving boundaries depart from uniform diffusion and require observations at several depths. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydrological diffusion time scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days.","failure":"常見誤解：「水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水文傳遞時間尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydrological diffusion time scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-09-k1","title":"水文傳遞時間尺度","titleEn":"Hydrological diffusion time scale","text":"降雨與庫水位會透過不同通道影響孔壓，擴散時間約隨距離平方增加，因此深層反應可能晚於地表事件。特徵時間只給量級，裂縫對流、非飽和入滲與變動邊界均會偏離均質擴散；應用多深度觀測區分傳遞機制。","textEn":"Rainfall and reservoir stage influence pressures through different pathways. A diffusion time scale grows with distance squared, so deep response may lag surface forcing.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水文傳遞時間尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hydrological diffusion time scale\" is correct?","options":["降雨與庫水位會透過不同通道影響孔壓，擴散時間約隨距離平方增加，因此深層反應可能晚於地表事件。","水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數","測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準"],"optionsEn":["Rainfall and reservoir stage influence pressures through different pathways.","The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown","A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference"],"answer":0,"explanation":"降雨與庫水位會透過不同通道影響孔壓，擴散時間約隨距離平方增加，因此深層反應可能晚於地表事件。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Rainfall and reservoir stage influence pressures through different pathways. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b243-v15-10","title":"水文傳遞時間尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Hydrological diffusion time scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水文傳遞時間尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydrological diffusion time scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水文傳遞時間尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hydrological diffusion time scale\", which statement holds?","options":["雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移","原創教學假設：LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days。","平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率"],"optionsEn":["Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement","Original teaching assumptions: LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days.","Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: LengthScale=20 m; hydraulicDiffusivity=0.002 m2/s; characteristicTime=20**2/0.002/86400=2.31481 days. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b243-v15-11","title":"水文傳遞時間尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrological diffusion time scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水文傳遞時間尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydrological diffusion time scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水文傳遞時間尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hydrological diffusion time scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序","比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures","Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b243-v15-12","title":"水文傳遞時間尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hydrological diffusion time scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水文傳遞時間尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydrological diffusion time scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較不同深度孔壓峰值時差並保留降雨強度與庫水位紀錄，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare pressure-peak delays by depth alongside rainfall intensity and reservoir-stage records. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水文傳遞時間尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hydrological diffusion time scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準"],"optionsEn":["Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把相關時差直接當因果證明可能漏掉共同季節驅動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating correlation lag as causation can overlook a common seasonal driver. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b243-v15-13","title":"測斜積分與基準：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Inclinometer integration and reference: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「測斜積分與基準」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Inclinometer integration and reference” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"測斜儀以各段傾角積分得到水平位移，底端固定假設與套管方向是必要邊界。局部剪切會集中在少數深度，而整根套管轉動可能呈現平滑曲線；需要反向讀值與穩定基準，不能把積分結果一律解釋成滑面位移。 驗證時應核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度，並辨識以下失效情境：底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測斜積分與基準」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An inclinometer integrates segment inclinations into lateral displacement. A fixed toe and known casing orientation are essential boundaries. Local shear concentrates at limited depths, whereas rotation of the whole casing may produce a smooth curve; opposite-face readings and an independent stable reference distinguish these mechanisms. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Inclinometer integration and reference” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測斜積分與基準」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Inclinometer integration and reference”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-13-k1","title":"測斜積分與基準","titleEn":"Inclinometer integration and reference","text":"測斜儀以各段傾角積分得到水平位移，底端固定假設與套管方向是必要邊界。局部剪切會集中在少數深度，而整根套管轉動可能呈現平滑曲線；需要反向讀值與穩定基準，不能把積分結果一律解釋成滑面位移。","textEn":"An inclinometer integrates segment inclinations into lateral displacement. A fixed toe and known casing orientation are essential boundaries.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測斜積分與基準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Inclinometer integration and reference\" is correct?","options":["測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準","測斜儀以各段傾角積分得到水平位移，底端固定假設與套管方向是必要邊界。","相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference","An inclinometer integrates segment inclinations into lateral displacement.","Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"測斜儀以各段傾角積分得到水平位移，底端固定假設與套管方向是必要邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An inclinometer integrates segment inclinations into lateral displacement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b243-v15-14","title":"測斜積分與基準：定量估算","titleEn":"Inclinometer integration and reference: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測斜積分與基準」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Inclinometer integration and reference” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測斜積分與基準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Inclinometer integration and reference\", which statement holds?","options":["短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻","只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度","原創教學假設：Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m。"],"optionsEn":["Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure","Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height","Original teaching assumptions: Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Ten identical segments: segmentLength=0.50 m; angleChange=0.20 degrees; lateralChange=10*0.50*sin(0.20 degrees)=0.0174533 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b243-v15-15","title":"測斜積分與基準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Inclinometer integration and reference: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測斜積分與基準」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Inclinometer integration and reference” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測斜積分與基準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Inclinometer integration and reference\"?","options":["核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低"],"optionsEn":["Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b243-v15-16","title":"測斜積分與基準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Inclinometer integration and reference: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測斜積分與基準」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Inclinometer integration and reference” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. Diagnose it by the following check: Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對正反向探測閉合及底端穩定性並檢查位移集中深度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. Diagnose it by the following check: Check opposite-face consistency and toe stability, then identify depths of concentrated displacement. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測斜積分與基準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Inclinometer integration and reference\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量。","相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation.","Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"底端隨滑體移動會低估整體平移量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A toe moving with the slide underestimates bulk translation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b243-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「衛星定位共同誤差」與「雷達視線投影」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"GNSS common-mode errors\" and \"Radar line-of-sight projection\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b243-v15-17","title":"衛星定位共同誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"GNSS common-mode errors: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「衛星定位共同誤差」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “GNSS common-mode errors” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"衛星定位能量測表面三維位移，但參考站漂移與共同大氣誤差會投影到所有測點。相對位移有助辨認坡體內部變形，卻可能消去真實共同平移；應同時保留絕對與相對解，並以坡外穩定點驗證參考框架。 驗證時應將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖，並辨識以下失效情境：移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「衛星定位共同誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"GNSS provides three-dimensional surface displacement, but reference-station drift and shared atmospheric errors affect many points together. Relative motion helps reveal internal deformation yet can remove genuine common translation. Preserve absolute and relative solutions and test the reference frame using stable off-slope monuments. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “GNSS common-mode errors” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「衛星定位共同誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “GNSS common-mode errors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-17-k1","title":"衛星定位共同誤差","titleEn":"GNSS common-mode errors","text":"衛星定位能量測表面三維位移，但參考站漂移與共同大氣誤差會投影到所有測點。相對位移有助辨認坡體內部變形，卻可能消去真實共同平移；應同時保留絕對與相對解，並以坡外穩定點驗證參考框架。","textEn":"GNSS provides three-dimensional surface displacement, but reference-station drift and shared atmospheric errors affect many points together. Relative motion helps reveal internal deformation yet can remove genuine common translation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「衛星定位共同誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"GNSS common-mode errors\" is correct?","options":["相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移","雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移","衛星定位能量測表面三維位移，但參考站漂移與共同大氣誤差會投影到所有測點。"],"optionsEn":["Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated","Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement","GNSS provides three-dimensional surface displacement, but reference-station drift and shared atmospheric errors affect many points together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"衛星定位能量測表面三維位移，但參考站漂移與共同大氣誤差會投影到所有測點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"GNSS provides three-dimensional surface displacement, but reference-station drift and shared atmospheric errors affect many points together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b243-v15-18","title":"衛星定位共同誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"GNSS common-mode errors: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「衛星定位共同誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “GNSS common-mode errors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「衛星定位共同誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"GNSS common-mode errors\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm。","平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率","提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm.","Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer","Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PointA=18 mm; pointB=11 mm in same axis and epoch; relativeMotion=18-11=7 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b243-v15-19","title":"衛星定位共同誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"GNSS common-mode errors: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「衛星定位共同誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “GNSS common-mode errors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「衛星定位共同誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"GNSS common-mode errors\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖。","示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations.","An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b243-v15-20","title":"衛星定位共同誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"GNSS common-mode errors: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「衛星定位共同誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “GNSS common-mode errors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移。診斷時應採取以下查核：將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. Diagnose it by the following check: Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移。診斷時應採取以下查核：將坡外基準站與坡內測點的共同訊號和相對變形分別繪圖，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. Diagnose it by the following check: Plot shared signals and relative deformation separately using off-slope reference stations. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「衛星定位共同誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"GNSS common-mode errors\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移","移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement","A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移動的參考站會使整坡出現假性反向位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A moving reference station creates an apparent opposite movement across the slope. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b243-v15-21","title":"雷達視線投影：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Radar line-of-sight projection: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「雷達視線投影」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Radar line-of-sight projection” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雷達干涉測量主要觀察衛星視線方向的位移投影，不能直接稱為垂直沉陷或最大滑動。只有在運動方向已知時才能用投影角回算幅值；植被失相干、大氣延遲與解纏錯誤仍需地面儀器交叉確認。 驗證時應以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致，並辨識以下失效情境：視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雷達視線投影」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Radar interferometry measures displacement projected onto the viewing line, not automatically vertical settlement or maximum movement. Recover magnitude from a projection angle only when motion direction is independently known. Vegetation decorrelation, atmospheric delay and phase-unwrapping errors require ground-based checks before interpreting a trend. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Radar line-of-sight projection” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雷達視線投影」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Radar line-of-sight projection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-21-k1","title":"雷達視線投影","titleEn":"Radar line-of-sight projection","text":"雷達干涉測量主要觀察衛星視線方向的位移投影，不能直接稱為垂直沉陷或最大滑動。只有在運動方向已知時才能用投影角回算幅值；植被失相干、大氣延遲與解纏錯誤仍需地面儀器交叉確認。","textEn":"Radar interferometry measures displacement projected onto the viewing line, not automatically vertical settlement or maximum movement. Recover magnitude from a projection angle only when motion direction is independently known.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雷達視線投影」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Radar line-of-sight projection\" is correct?","options":["雷達干涉測量主要觀察衛星視線方向的位移投影，不能直接稱為垂直沉陷或最大滑動。","雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移","短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻"],"optionsEn":["Radar interferometry measures displacement projected onto the viewing line, not automatically vertical settlement or maximum movement.","Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement","Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"雷達干涉測量主要觀察衛星視線方向的位移投影，不能直接稱為垂直沉陷或最大滑動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Radar interferometry measures displacement projected onto the viewing line, not automatically vertical settlement or maximum movement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b243-v15-22","title":"雷達視線投影：定量估算","titleEn":"Radar line-of-sight projection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雷達視線投影」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Radar line-of-sight projection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雷達視線投影」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Radar line-of-sight projection\", which statement holds?","options":["只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度","原創教學假設：Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm。","庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低"],"optionsEn":["Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height","Original teaching assumptions: Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm.","Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Known motion direction30 degrees from radar LOS; LOSmovement=12 mm; motionMagnitude=12/cos(30 degrees)=13.8564 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b243-v15-23","title":"雷達視線投影：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Radar line-of-sight projection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雷達視線投影」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Radar line-of-sight projection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雷達視線投影」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Radar line-of-sight projection\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數","以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown","Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b243-v15-24","title":"雷達視線投影：失效診斷","titleEn":"Radar line-of-sight projection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雷達視線投影」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Radar line-of-sight projection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差。診斷時應採取以下查核：以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差。診斷時應採取以下查核：以不同衛星軌道與地面三維定位比較方向投影是否一致，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare projections from different satellite tracks with three-dimensional ground positioning. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雷達視線投影」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Radar line-of-sight projection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻"],"optionsEn":["Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"視線近乎垂直運動方向時小量雜訊會放大反算誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Near-perpendicular viewing greatly amplifies noise in recovered movement magnitude. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b243-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「位移速率與加速度」與「水位降速與內水頭」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Displacement rate and acceleration\" and \"Drawdown rate and internal head\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b243-v15-25","title":"位移速率與加速度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Displacement rate and acceleration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「位移速率與加速度」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Displacement rate and acceleration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"差分位移可以揭露速率變化，卻同時放大量測雜訊；採樣間隔改變也會造成表觀加速。應使用相同時間窗與誤差模型，不把短期兩點差分外推成失穩日期；若降雨、溫度或施工改變，需分段解釋驅動條件。 驗證時應以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點，並辨識以下失效情境：不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「位移速率與加速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Differencing displacement reveals rate changes but also amplifies noise. Changing observation intervals can create apparent acceleration. Use consistent windows and an uncertainty model rather than extrapolating two points into a failure date; interpret separate periods when rainfall, temperature or construction alters the driving conditions. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Displacement rate and acceleration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2.","failure":"常見誤解：「短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「位移速率與加速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Displacement rate and acceleration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-25-k1","title":"位移速率與加速度","titleEn":"Displacement rate and acceleration","text":"差分位移可以揭露速率變化，卻同時放大量測雜訊；採樣間隔改變也會造成表觀加速。應使用相同時間窗與誤差模型，不把短期兩點差分外推成失穩日期；若降雨、溫度或施工改變，需分段解釋驅動條件。","textEn":"Differencing displacement reveals rate changes but also amplifies noise. Changing observation intervals can create apparent acceleration.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「位移速率與加速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Displacement rate and acceleration\" is correct?","options":["短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻","差分位移可以揭露速率變化，卻同時放大量測雜訊；採樣間隔改變也會造成表觀加速。","平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率"],"optionsEn":["Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure","Differencing displacement reveals rate changes but also amplifies noise.","Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer"],"answer":1,"explanation":"差分位移可以揭露速率變化，卻同時放大量測雜訊；採樣間隔改變也會造成表觀加速。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Differencing displacement reveals rate changes but also amplifies noise. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b243-v15-26","title":"位移速率與加速度：定量估算","titleEn":"Displacement rate and acceleration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「位移速率與加速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Displacement rate and acceleration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「位移速率與加速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Displacement rate and acceleration\", which statement holds?","options":["提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序","示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全","原創教學假設：Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2。"],"optionsEn":["Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures","An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope","Original teaching assumptions: Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Successive daily rates=2 and5 mm/day; elapsed=3 days; meanAcceleration=(5-2)/3=1 mm/day2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b243-v15-27","title":"位移速率與加速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Displacement rate and acceleration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「位移速率與加速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Displacement rate and acceleration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「位移速率與加速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Displacement rate and acceleration\"?","options":["以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準"],"optionsEn":["Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b243-v15-28","title":"位移速率與加速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Displacement rate and acceleration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「位移速率與加速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Displacement rate and acceleration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度。診斷時應採取以下查核：以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. Diagnose it by the following check: Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度。診斷時應採取以下查核：以相同時間窗重算速度並確認加速也出現在獨立測點，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. Diagnose it by the following check: Recalculate rates over common windows and confirm acceleration at independent points. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「位移速率與加速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Displacement rate and acceleration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度。","平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration.","Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不等間隔差分未除以時間會產生假的加速度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unequal-interval differences without time normalization generate false acceleration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b243-v15-29","title":"水位降速與內水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drawdown rate and internal head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「水位降速與內水頭」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drawdown rate and internal head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水庫調降速度與坡體排水速度不匹配時，外部支撐及內部有效應力會同時改變。以平均日降幅描述調度不代表孔壓已達平衡；需要把停降段與持續降段分開，並比較滑面附近與坡腳測點的不同反應。 驗證時應對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散，並辨識以下失效情境：把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水位降速與內水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When drawdown outpaces slope drainage, external support and internal effective stress change differently. Mean daily drawdown does not establish pressure equilibrium. Separate holding periods from continued lowering and compare observations near the potential slip surface with those at the toe to identify spatially different responses. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drawdown rate and internal head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水位降速與內水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drawdown rate and internal head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-29-k1","title":"水位降速與內水頭","titleEn":"Drawdown rate and internal head","text":"水庫調降速度與坡體排水速度不匹配時，外部支撐及內部有效應力會同時改變。以平均日降幅描述調度不代表孔壓已達平衡；需要把停降段與持續降段分開，並比較滑面附近與坡腳測點的不同反應。","textEn":"When drawdown outpaces slope drainage, external support and internal effective stress change differently. Mean daily drawdown does not establish pressure equilibrium.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水位降速與內水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drawdown rate and internal head\" is correct?","options":["平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率","只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度","水庫調降速度與坡體排水速度不匹配時，外部支撐及內部有效應力會同時改變。"],"optionsEn":["Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer","Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height","When drawdown outpaces slope drainage, external support and internal effective stress change differently."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水庫調降速度與坡體排水速度不匹配時，外部支撐及內部有效應力會同時改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When drawdown outpaces slope drainage, external support and internal effective stress change differently. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b243-v15-30","title":"水位降速與內水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Drawdown rate and internal head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水位降速與內水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drawdown rate and internal head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水位降速與內水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drawdown rate and internal head\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m。","庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低","水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m.","Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction","The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: ReservoirFalls=6 m in4 days; internalHeadFalls=2 m in4 days; additionalHeadLag=6-2=4 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b243-v15-31","title":"水位降速與內水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drawdown rate and internal head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水位降速與內水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drawdown rate and internal head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水位降速與內水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drawdown rate and internal head\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散。","相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold.","Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b243-v15-32","title":"水位降速與內水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drawdown rate and internal head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水位降速與內水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drawdown rate and internal head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後。診斷時應採取以下查核：對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均洩降速率就是每一土層的排水速率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mean reservoir drawdown rate equals drainage rate in every layer\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後。診斷時應採取以下查核：對照庫水位與滑面孔壓下降量並檢查停降後是否繼續消散，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare reservoir and slip-surface head reductions and observe continued dissipation during a hold. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水位降速與內水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drawdown rate and internal head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度","把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height","Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把庫水位當全坡內水頭會忽略快速洩降的不利滯後。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting reservoir stage for all internal heads ignores adverse rapid-drawdown lag. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b243-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「潛在滑體與影響範圍」與「監測不確定與應變」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Potential slide volume and consequences\" and \"Monitoring uncertainty and response\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b243-v15-33","title":"潛在滑體與影響範圍：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Potential slide volume and consequences: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「潛在滑體與影響範圍」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Potential slide volume and consequences” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滑體幾何是後果分析的起點，但體積本身不能決定湧浪高度；入水速度、深度、滑體形狀與水庫幾何也重要。用簡化稜柱估體積應清楚標示平均厚度假設，再以地質界面、地形與鑽探檢驗範圍，避免把包絡體積當精確崩塌量。 驗證時應用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度，並辨識以下失效情境：把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潛在滑體與影響範圍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Slide geometry begins consequence assessment, but volume alone does not determine wave height. Entry velocity, depth, shape and reservoir geometry also matter. A prism estimate must state its average-thickness assumption and be checked against geology, terrain and boreholes rather than presented as an exact failure volume. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Potential slide volume and consequences” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「潛在滑體與影響範圍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Potential slide volume and consequences”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-33-k1","title":"潛在滑體與影響範圍","titleEn":"Potential slide volume and consequences","text":"滑體幾何是後果分析的起點，但體積本身不能決定湧浪高度；入水速度、深度、滑體形狀與水庫幾何也重要。用簡化稜柱估體積應清楚標示平均厚度假設，再以地質界面、地形與鑽探檢驗範圍，避免把包絡體積當精確崩塌量。","textEn":"Slide geometry begins consequence assessment, but volume alone does not determine wave height. Entry velocity, depth, shape and reservoir geometry also matter.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潛在滑體與影響範圍」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Potential slide volume and consequences\" is correct?","options":["滑體幾何是後果分析的起點，但體積本身不能決定湧浪高度；入水速度、深度、滑體形狀與水庫幾何也重要。","只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度","提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序"],"optionsEn":["Slide geometry begins consequence assessment, but volume alone does not determine wave height.","Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height","Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures"],"answer":0,"explanation":"滑體幾何是後果分析的起點，但體積本身不能決定湧浪高度；入水速度、深度、滑體形狀與水庫幾何也重要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Slide geometry begins consequence assessment, but volume alone does not determine wave height. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b243-v15-34","title":"潛在滑體與影響範圍：定量估算","titleEn":"Potential slide volume and consequences: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「潛在滑體與影響範圍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Potential slide volume and consequences” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潛在滑體與影響範圍」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Potential slide volume and consequences\", which statement holds?","options":["示意安全係數足以核准複雜邊坡安全","原創教學假設：PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3。","測斜孔底只要夠深就一定是固定基準"],"optionsEn":["An illustrative factor of safety approves a complex slope","Original teaching assumptions: PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3.","A sufficiently deep inclinometer toe is always a fixed reference"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PlanArea=18000 m2; assumedMeanThickness=12 m; prismVolume=18000*12=216000 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b243-v15-35","title":"潛在滑體與影響範圍：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Potential slide volume and consequences: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「潛在滑體與影響範圍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Potential slide volume and consequences” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潛在滑體與影響範圍」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Potential slide volume and consequences\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","雷達視線位移可以直接當成垂直位移","用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Radar line-of-sight displacement directly equals vertical displacement","Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b243-v15-36","title":"潛在滑體與影響範圍：失效診斷","titleEn":"Potential slide volume and consequences: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「潛在滑體與影響範圍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Potential slide volume and consequences” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積。診斷時應採取以下查核：用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. Diagnose it by the following check: Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只知道滑體體積就能決定入庫湧浪高度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Slide volume alone determines reservoir impulse-wave height\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積。診斷時應採取以下查核：用鑽孔與地表裂縫約束滑面深度並對厚度範圍做敏感度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. Diagnose it by the following check: Constrain slip depth with boreholes and surface cracks and vary the thickness range. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潛在滑體與影響範圍」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Potential slide volume and consequences\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序"],"optionsEn":["Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把最大厚度套用整個面積會系統高估稜柱體積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying maximum thickness over the entire area systematically overestimates prism volume. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b243-v15-37","title":"監測不確定與應變：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and response: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「監測不確定與應變」如何影響水庫邊坡穩定監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Monitoring uncertainty and response” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-slope stability monitoring”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"儀器雜訊、基準誤差與空間代表性共同影響警戒解釋；兩個獨立時點差值的誤差不是單次精度。以合成標準不確定度可判斷訊號相對雜訊，但工程應變還需失效模式、資料可用率與既定責任鏈，不能僅依統計倍數自動停工。 驗證時應將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程，並辨識以下失效情境：沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「監測不確定與應變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Noise, reference errors and spatial representativeness influence alerts. The uncertainty of a difference between independent epochs is not one-epoch precision. Combined standard uncertainty describes signal relative to noise, while response also depends on failure modes, data availability and assigned responsibilities rather than an automatic statistical multiplier. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Monitoring uncertainty and response” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「監測不確定與應變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Monitoring uncertainty and response”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-37-k1","title":"監測不確定與應變","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and response","text":"儀器雜訊、基準誤差與空間代表性共同影響警戒解釋；兩個獨立時點差值的誤差不是單次精度。以合成標準不確定度可判斷訊號相對雜訊，但工程應變還需失效模式、資料可用率與既定責任鏈，不能僅依統計倍數自動停工。","textEn":"Noise, reference errors and spatial representativeness influence alerts. The uncertainty of a difference between independent epochs is not one-epoch precision.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「監測不確定與應變」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Monitoring uncertainty and response\" is correct?","options":["提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序","儀器雜訊、基準誤差與空間代表性共同影響警戒解釋；兩個獨立時點差值的誤差不是單次精度。","庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低"],"optionsEn":["Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures","Noise, reference errors and spatial representativeness influence alerts.","Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"儀器雜訊、基準誤差與空間代表性共同影響警戒解釋；兩個獨立時點差值的誤差不是單次精度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Noise, reference errors and spatial representativeness influence alerts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b243-v15-38","title":"監測不確定與應變：定量估算","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and response: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「監測不確定與應變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Monitoring uncertainty and response” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「監測不確定與應變」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Monitoring uncertainty and response\", which statement holds?","options":["水文特徵時間就是可精確預報的崩塌倒數","相對位移很小就表示整個坡體沒有平移","原創教學假設：Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm。"],"optionsEn":["The hydrological characteristic time is a precise failure countdown","Small relative motion proves that the whole slope has not translated","Original teaching assumptions: Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Independent epoch standard uncertainties=2 and2 mm; displacementChangeU=sqrt(2**2+2**2)=2.82843 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b243-v15-39","title":"監測不確定與應變：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and response: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「監測不確定與應變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Monitoring uncertainty and response” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「監測不確定與應變」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Monitoring uncertainty and response\"?","options":["將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","短期加速足以決定精確的邊坡失穩時刻"],"optionsEn":["Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Short-term acceleration determines the exact time of slope failure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b243-v15-40","title":"監測不確定與應變：失效診斷","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and response: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"prerequisiteIds":["b243-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「監測不確定與應變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Monitoring uncertainty and response” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置。診斷時應採取以下查核：將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. Diagnose it by the following check: Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「提升量測精密度就不需要工程應變程序」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher measurement precision removes the need for response procedures\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b243-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置。診斷時應採取以下查核：將共同基準偏差另列並以演練檢查警報到現場回報的流程，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. Diagnose it by the following check: Separate shared reference bias and exercise the process from alarm to field confirmation. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]},{"id":"b243-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「監測不確定與應變」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Monitoring uncertainty and response\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置。","庫水位降低就保證坡內孔壓同時降低"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action.","Falling reservoir stage guarantees simultaneous internal pore-pressure reduction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"沒有現場回報閉環的警報可能持續失去實際處置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An alarm without field-confirmation feedback can remain disconnected from action. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-slopes","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usgs-slopes","v15s-usgs-guobu"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
